# Commercial S12.1 final-review diagnosis — runtime environment, bundle restore and nginx order

Date: 2026-09-30

## Finding

Same-SHA review of Control `c69b2cdc91f1d4f572081a9e555863303b030862`
identified three release-contract gaps before merge or server mutation:

1. the credential-bearing unit still executed the canonical Application venv,
   outside the root-private immutable release tree;
2. backup bundles were verified but not imported during rollback, so a pruned
   otherwise-unreachable detached HEAD could not be restored; and
3. rollback reloaded restored nginx only after repository recovery, allowing a
   Git-recovery failure to leave the temporary callback route loaded.

No server deployment had begun. The exactly-once runtime attempt therefore
remained unused.

## Root cause

The first immutable-stage correction protected Application and Control Git
material but treated the interpreter environment as an unchanged host
dependency. The rollback contract similarly proved bundle creation without
making the bundle the authoritative object source, and grouped nginx reload
with final service housekeeping rather than the first safety restoration.

## Versioned correction

- Materialize the complete canonical venv into the root-private stage,
  dereference file symlinks, retain only internal relative directory symlinks,
  reject escaping links/special files, compare source-before/source-after/staged
  SHA-256, enforce the exact locked dependency
  versions, remove all write bits and bind interpreter plus venv hashes in an
  immutable environment record. systemd executes only the staged Python.
- Create bundles from explicit `HEAD` plus all refs. Before restore checkout,
  verify the recorded bundle digest, verify and unbundle it through the
  quarantined Git directory, and prove commit/tree/tip object types.
- Validate and reload restored nginx immediately after restoring its files and
  before entering repository recovery. `daemon-reload` remains after the
  repository barrier because it is unrelated to removing the public callback.

## Regression proof

The focused contract suite now covers an unrelated detached commit that is
removed by reflog expiry and `git gc --prune=now`, then restored only from the
verified bundle. It also builds and hardens a synthetic venv, proves canonical
repository drift cannot affect the staged source/runtime, and rejects staged
interpreter-byte drift. Rollback ordering asserts nginx test/reload precede the
repository barrier and completion marker.

## Rollback

The existing exactly-once backup-first rollback remains authoritative. It
stops the runtime, removes the root-private stage, restores the exact files,
reloads the nginx baseline first, restores repositories from the verified
bundles under atomic barriers, reloads systemd and writes the completion marker
only after durable repository sync. Credentials are never copied or emitted.
